  fydroid runs each app in its own freeform window composited by Chrome.
  On a cold first launch (no saved window bounds) the WM app-open transition
  animates the freeform window in; fydroid forwards the mid-animation surface
  size to Chrome, Chrome echoes it back, and onGeometryChanged resizes the
  Android task to that transient size — which then sticks (clamped to the
  220dp resizable-task minimum), so the window opens far too narrow.

  WindowManagerService falls back to config_appTransitionAnimationDuration-
  ScaleDefault when TRANSITION_ANIMATION_SCALE is unset (it is never seeded
  into the settings DB). Default it to 0 so the open transition is instant —
  no transient frames are composited/forwarded, and the window opens at its
  proper size. Only the transition scale is affected; window_animation_scale
  and animator_duration_scale keep their stock 1.0 defaults.
-->
<resources>
    <item name="config_appTransitionAnimationDurationScaleDefault" format="float" type="dimen">0.0</item>

    <!--
      WeChat (and other apps) call AppWidgetManager.getInstance(ctx).getAppWidgetIds()
      right after account initialization and assume a non-null manager. getInstance()
      returns null unless the framework's AppWidgetService is started, which crashes
      such apps with:
        NullPointerException: Attempt to invoke virtual method
        'int[] AppWidgetManager.getAppWidgetIds(ComponentName)' on a null object reference
          at com.tencent.mm.plugin.appbrand.app.r9.onAccountInitialized(...)

      ARC advertises android.software.app_widgets as an unavailable-feature (no
      home-screen widget hosting) but still expects the service ENABLED via this
      bool — see permissions/cheets.xml and b/110122867. The framework default is
      false, so enable it here: AppWidgetService starts, getInstance() is non-null,
      getAppWidgetIds() returns an empty array, and the app no longer crashes. The
      feature stays unavailable, so nothing offers to place home-screen widgets.
    -->
    <bool name="config_enableAppWidgetService">true</bool>
</resources>
